Common Interview Answer

What is a Layer 7 Policy in Cilium?

Layer 7 policies allow traffic control based on application-level information such as HTTP methods, URL paths, DNS queries, gRPC methods, and Kafka topics. Unlike standard Kubernetes NetworkPolicies, which operate at Layers 3 and 4, Cilium can enforce application-aware security policies using eBPF together with protocol-aware proxies.

Easy Interview Memory
