Kubernetes Native NetworkPolicy is a standard Kubernetes resource used to control Pod-to-Pod and Pod-to-external traffic at Layers 3 and 4. Kubernetes defines the policy object, but enforcement is performed by the CNI plugin such as Cilium or Calico. Native NetworkPolicies can filter traffic based on pod selectors, namespace selectors, IP blocks, and ports, but they cannot enforce Layer 7 application-aware rules such as HTTP methods or URL paths. For Layer 7 enforcement, solutions like CiliumNetworkPolicy are used.
